# What ran before a step in an arm is what ran before its choice and what ran before it in its own arm (#329): the
# shelf is set up in the arm that keeps anything, and the report is kept in an arm of a choice inside that arm. A choice
# is a coproduct of its arms, and the arm `KEEP` is the composite `open_shelf ; (keep_report + 1)`: the choice of
# `REPORT` is a coproduct inside that arm, a frame of its own in it, never another arm beside it (#357). Both calls run
# in one run where `REPORT` holds: the set-up stands before the report in the arm both are in. It ran before
# `keep_report`, and `write` under it writes the report in `out`, the folder the set-up decides. The shelf is made in the
# outer arm and taken in the inner one, so it stands in the outer choice's frame. The plans of the same program in Rust
# and TypeScript say the same (`rust.plan`, `typescript.plan`).

route arms.main
choice main/?1                                     # `if KEEP:`
step main/?1/open_shelf
step main/?1/open_shelf/Shelf()
choice main/?1/?1                                  # `if REPORT:`, inside the arm of `KEEP`
step main/?1/?1/Shelf.keep_report
step main/?1/?1/Shelf.keep_report/write

line entry > main call
line main/?1/open_shelf/Shelf() > Shelf@main/?1/open_shelf/Shelf() value
line Shelf@main/?1/open_shelf/Shelf() > main/?1/open_shelf value
line main/?1/open_shelf > Shelf·shelf@main/?1/open_shelf value
line Shelf·shelf@main/?1/open_shelf > main/?1/?1/Shelf.keep_report/write value     # `write(self.root / "report.txt", text)`
line main/?1/?1/Shelf.keep_report/write > File(out/report.txt) own

home Shelf@main/?1/open_shelf/Shelf() main/?1/open_shelf
home Shelf·shelf@main/?1/open_shelf main/?1

side entry left
side File(out/report.txt) right
